@Janpot it seems MacOS has a shorter limit for socket paths length (104 bytes) than Linux. We could place the socket in the global tmp directory, or we could try to reduce the length of the path within `.next/`. Any preference to which we do?

We could place it in `.next/di/s/t.sock`(di = docs-infra, s = sockets, t = types) or `.next/docs-infra/types.sock` or `/tmp/{hashOfNextjsProjectDir}`

Edit: I went with `.next/docs-infra/types.sock` as it's 40 bytes shorter than before and that seems to keep us well below the 104 byte limit (in your case 66 bytes instead of 106).

